# Local high-volume art library
#
# These folders are Unity import targets for locally synchronised production
# assets. Keep their contents (including Unity-generated .meta files) out of
# normal Git history. The tracked README describes the required layout.
#
# A clone therefore needs a separate asset-library sync before it can use
# production models/textures. Do not commit WorldSpawnCatalog references to
# assets from these ignored folders.
/Assets/_Game/Models/Ready/*
!/Assets/_Game/Models/Ready/README.md
/Assets/_Game/Textures/Ready/
/Assets/_Game/Art/Source/
/Assets/_Game/Art/Imported/TerrainStarter_v001/

# Keep meta files tracked once Unity creates them
!*.meta

# The local-art exception must be repeated after the global meta exception.
# Keep only the Ready folder's README tracked; Unity regenerates its metadata
# locally after the external asset library has been synchronised.
/Assets/_Game/Models.meta
/Assets/_Game/Models/Ready.meta
/Assets/_Game/Models/Ready/*.meta
/Assets/_Game/Textures.meta
/Assets/_Game/Textures/Ready.meta
/Assets/_Game/Art/Source.meta
